  partName: Cylinder Head (2)
  description: The Cylinder Head (2) is a critical component located at the top-center-center
    of the rocket engine, playing a crucial role in managing the combustion process
    by regulating the flow of fuel and air into the engine's cylinders. Its large
    and complex shape is designed to withstand the high pressures and temperatures
    generated during combustion. Interestingly, the cylinder head is typically made
    from a high-strength, heat-resistant material to ensure optimal performance and
    durability.
